    <p>The post names Vals, Harvey’s Legal Agent Benchmark, and Gray Swan without a number. Those stay off this card.</p>
    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Access and pricing</h2>
    <p>Since 13 October 2026, Google says Argon is available globally in these places:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Developers: the paid tier of the Gemini API, in Google AI Studio and Android Studio. Google AI Ultra subscribers can also try it in AI Studio and Google Antigravity, Google’s agent coding tool.</li>
      <li>Businesses: Gemini for business, the API, and Google Antigravity.</li>
      <li>Everyday users: the Gemini app and AI Mode in Search, for Google AI Pro and Ultra subscribers.</li>
      <li>Cyber defenders: Google says vetted defenders can apply to the Fairwind Program to get Argon without cyber guardrails, and that it is expanding the program to hundreds more partners.</li>
    </ul>
